    <solution><p>For all of the points, we determine if the function value <m>f</m> is
positive, negative, or zero by whether the point is plotted above,
below, or on the <m>x</m>-axis.  The sign of <m>f'</m> is determined by
the slope of the function at the point: if the function is increasing,
then <m>f'&gt;0</m>; if it is decreasing, <m>f'\lt 0</m>, and if it is neither
increasing nor decreasing, then <m>f'=0</m>.  Similarly, the sign of
<m>f''</m> is determined by the concavity of the function: if the function
is concave up, then <m>f''&gt;0</m>, if it is concave down, <m>f''\lt 0</m>.  This
gives the table</p>
